    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d435">

                <pb facs="0574" n="563" xml:id="pg563"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 Poland/157</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-08">December 8, 1937</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Polish Ambassador called on no particular business, except to hand me a
                    letter, copy of which is attached,<anchor n="66" xml:id="d435-f1"/> in which the
                    Polish Government declines to make any payment on their debt.</p>
                <p>The Ambassador incidentally expressed renewed interest in the Jewish problem in
                    Poland and his deep interest in endeavoring to help solve it. He concluded by
                    saying that he believed the acute nature of the problem would subside very
                    soon.</p>
                <closer><signed>C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ordell</hi>] H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ull</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d435-f1" n="66" xml:id="d435-f1-content">
                <p>Department of State, <hi rendition="#italic">Press Releases</hi>, December 11,
